--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-reviewer-combined/feedback_reuse-scope-labels.md
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+---
+name: reuse-scope-labels
+description: a rule letting a recorded run substitute for a gate by its Scope label - check every run kind that can write that label (named test, name filter in a one-file suite)
+metadata:
+  type: feedback
+---
+
+When a rule lets a recorded test run stand in for a later gate because of its Scope label (e.g. `full` ≥ `impacted` reuse), list every run kind that can write that label, then check it against the gate's real selection.
+
+**Why:** a binary Scope (`full` or `impacted`) labels a single named-test run `impacted`, and the reuse rule then accepts it as the impacted-set gate. In a one-file suite (`tests/run.js`), a `--filter` run "selects every test file", so it can even be labelled `full` and skip the terminal full-suite run.
+
+**How to apply:** for each new writer of `Suite run` (a review-fix or in-place tester), ask what its narrowest allowed run records as Scope. Then read the consuming gate's reuse condition (impl-test step 8, the terminal-run reuse, the pr skip) and see whether that label passes it.
diff --git a/.claude/agent-memory/asd-reviewer-combined/reference_gh-base-repo-resolution.md b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-reviewer-combined/reference_gh-base-repo-resolution.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..793902f6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/agent-memory/asd-reviewer-combined/reference_gh-base-repo-resolution.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+name: gh-base-repo-resolution
+description: bare `gh repo view` / `gh issue` without -R follow gh's base-repo resolution (set-default, upstream > github > origin ranking, or an error with several remotes), never `origin` by definition
+metadata:
+  type: reference
+---
+
+Without an argument or `-R`, gh resolves the base repo from `gh repo set-default`, else by ranking remotes by name (`upstream` above `github` above `origin`); from v2.21 it errors with several remotes until a default is set. Sources: https://cli.github.com/manual/gh_repo_set-default, https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/9083.
+
+**How to apply:** when a rule or AC says "the repo of `origin`", a bare `gh repo view` does not implement it. Pass the URL: `git remote get-url origin`, then `gh repo view <url>`.
